
pltcav  is a script to plot cavitation polars from XFOIL easily, using gnuplot.
This takes the polar names as arg list and makes a plot to the screen and 
a postscript hardcopy "cav-plt.ps".   Saves the gnuplot commands to "gnuplt.cmd".   

The polars need to have Cpmin listed, which is enabled with the CINC toggle command in OPER.
Three sample such polars are here.  Plot them with the command line:

pltcav polar.e817mod1-rn6mn1 polar.h105-10a-rn6mn1 polar.db10c-rn6mn1

